    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89732" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσμάσσω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>knead</i> or <i>plaster</i> one thing <i>against</i>
			another: <i>apply, attach closely to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείλεσι χείλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					12.32
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σικύην τύψει</span> the
			cuppinginstrument to the snake-bite, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				922
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὸν Πειραιᾶ [τῇ
			πόλει</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				815
			</span></i>:—aor.
			
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τηλέφιλον ποτεμάξατο</span> (
				Dor.
			) <i>stuck to</i> [the arm], <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				3.29
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλευραῖσι προσμαχθέν</span>
			<i>stuck close</i> to his sides, of the poisoned robe, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				1053
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				1029
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηλῖδα προσμεμάχθαι τῇ ψυχῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VA</u>
					3.42
				</span></i>
			.</div>
